meta {
  name: Create Channel - Invalid Format (422)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/channels
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test Bad Format",
    "format": "NotARealFormat123"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
  res.body.errors[0].description: contains format
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08. Trigger case, creates nothing.

  ## Spec discrepancy found -- same pattern as Connections (Phase 1e)
  `ChannelCreateInputDto.format`'s spec description calls it a free
  string ("CSV, XLSX, XML, JSON, SHOPIFY, BIGCOMMERCE, etc." given only as
  examples). It's actually validated against a hidden fixed set:
  `{"data":[],"errors":[{"name":"ValidationError","description":"Field
  format is unknown"}]}`. Unlike Connections' equivalent error, this one
  does **not** enumerate the valid values in the message -- `CSV` and
  `XML` are both confirmed valid (see the other files in this folder);
  the full valid set wasn't exhaustively enumerated.
}
